{
  "id": "overt-response",
  "term": "overt response",
  "definition": "An overt response is an observable action or spoken output a person makes during a task, such as saying a word aloud. In this context, it contrasts with earlier mental processing that can be measured before the visible or audible response occurs.",
  "field": "cognition",
